/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
  VMFL003 -- turbulent pipe, standard k-epsilon, steady simpleFoam.

  The cell Peclet number based on the MOLECULAR viscosity is enormous
  (|u| dx / nu = 50 * (2/__NX__) / 1.4607346938775508e-05 ~ 2.7e7 at NX = 250),
  so a central div(phi,U) is out of the question: `bounded Gauss linearUpwind
  grad(U)` -- second order, stable -- is used, exactly as on VMFL005.

  The turbulence transport terms use `bounded Gauss limitedLinear 1`: second
  order where the solution is smooth, degrading to upwind where the limiter
  activates.  That is expected to happen ONLY in the entrance region (the first
  ~21.5 D of a 500 D pipe), and it is the reason PREREGISTRATION.md section 6
  registers an EXPECTED OBSERVED ORDER of p ~ 1 rather than p ~ 2 on the axial
  triple: the axial discretisation error of the gate quantity lives almost
  entirely in that limited entrance region, because over the remaining ~96 % of
  the pipe the flow is fully developed and the axial pressure variation is
  LINEAR and therefore represented exactly by any of the three meshes.

  `bounded` prepends -fvm::Sp(fvc::div(phi), X), the standard steady-state
  correction for a non-exactly-conservative intermediate phi.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
FoamFile
{
    version     2.0;
    format      ascii;
    class       dictionary;
    object      fvSchemes;
}
// * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * //

ddtSchemes
{
    default         steadyState;
}

gradSchemes
{
    default         Gauss linear;
}

divSchemes
{
    // `default Gauss linear` rather than `default none`: a div term this dict
    // does not name by the exact v2606 spelling then still runs with a
    // second-order scheme instead of aborting (the team's VMFL001/VMFL005
    // choice).  Every term simpleFoam+kEpsilon actually assembles is named
    // explicitly below.
    default         Gauss linear;
    div(phi,U)      bounded Gauss linearUpwind grad(U);
    div(phi,k)      bounded Gauss limitedLinear 1;
    div(phi,epsilon) bounded Gauss limitedLinear 1;
    div((nuEff*dev2(T(grad(U))))) Gauss linear;
}

laplacianSchemes
{
    default         Gauss linear corrected;
}

interpolationSchemes
{
    default         linear;
}

snGradSchemes
{
    default         corrected;
}

wallDist
{
    method          meshWave;
}

